Weird. According to `ls-remote`, eugene.adell/wireshark is reachable:

```
$ git ls-remote git@gitlab.com:eugene.adell/wireshark.git | tail -n5
893b5a5e1e3e925ea4f1ba408091c4af113538df	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.4^{}
90a34805f0ca346d5ec2cf07108cf7d8bebb5267	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.5
ed20ddea8138edeef2314d03a6b4a70312367446	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.5^{}
197ed3d7a19c4fab7a47198d64812d09f17b7747	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.6
4f9257fb8ccce92b519d87c4cc905107ae09b5e9	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.6^{}

$ git remote add eatest git@gitlab.com:eugene.adell/wireshark.git

$ git ls-remote eatest | tail -n5
893b5a5e1e3e925ea4f1ba408091c4af113538df	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.4^{}
90a34805f0ca346d5ec2cf07108cf7d8bebb5267	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.5
ed20ddea8138edeef2314d03a6b4a70312367446	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.5^{}
197ed3d7a19c4fab7a47198d64812d09f17b7747	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.6
4f9257fb8ccce92b519d87c4cc905107ae09b5e9	refs/tags/wireshark-3.2.6^{}
```

Can you try running `GIT_TRACE=1 git ls-remote git@gitlab.com:eugene.adell/wireshark.git`?

